. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. 
.         * We estimate a linear fixed effects model. Thus we analyze individua
> l within 
.         * variation in political preferences after becoming a parent to a dau
> ghter.
. 
.         * polit_index is measure of left-leaning political preferences normal
> ized to [0,1]
.         * 0 stands for the rightest, and 1 for the leftist preference on the 
> scale.
.         * We regress the preferences onto the age, migration background, voca
> tional
.         * education, East German affiliation, and sex of an individual for th
> e sake 
.         * of completeness. However, the estimates of constant variables will 
> be 
.         * omitted in the FE estimation. We use individual level cluster stand
> ard errors. 
.         
.         xtreg polit_index i.d_daughter c.age i.mig i.educ i.east i.female i.s
> year, fe vce(cluster pid)
